{"ts": 1791259872.3040981, "type": "step", "step": 20, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Totally fine \u2014 here\u2019s the key idea in one line: pass^k means the system succeeds on every one of k attempts, not just at least one. So if you test 3 seeds, pass^3 = 1 only if all 3 succeed; otherwise pass^3 = 0. For your writeup, the eval section should say what counted as success, which 3 seeds you used, and whether all 3 passed. After you finish the short reading, send me your own 1-sentence definition of pass^k and I\u2019ll help turn it into writeup text.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\n[activity] t=8 messages 4m", "t": 12, "activity": [{"t": 8, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.5037622850952317}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9287143533309796, "motivation": 0.3816049256110158, "reliance": 0.3682647873598394, "persistence": 0.43018974832101986, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
